editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:311:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: the steading's woman's last word is about HEALERS ("Healer would've had it straight in an hour." / "There isn't one." / "There's not. They stop inside, where the tiers are."), Lira says "There isn't one", and nobody asks the woman about ranks; the thought that ranks stop there too is Lira's own, said at the fire. Cael learns of the bite when his left foot drags and he sits down in the river (Seln sees it first; no blood in the water). The finding begins as a line of Cael's own, which Karis strikes and replaces by dictation. The day-57 log gives no "earned" figure; Thornwater's yard has no stride count; Hesk's letter is known by its fold. Owner flag 5 above is superseded by the coordinator's amendment. Word counts, metrics, line numbers and the protected-units table elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the repaired chapter 13 also carries the protected three-speech unit at lines 35–41.*
