editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:441:- **The line (OWNER-pending #49, default in force).** At the line the five live Arbiters stop at the same step: Karis's, Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's. Cael's own Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling and nothing in him changes there; his fragments go on answering inside. The protected log entries are word for word (their loose "mine" is his shorthand). Outside them nothing says "his Path", nothing says his Arbiter is awake or unaffected, and nothing says WHY the fragments answer. The word *Quieting* has not been said. "Compact" has not been said aloud: the stake carries the registry stamp. "Made" has been said of the place once, by Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:443:- **Ring geometry — the manuscript governs (Movement 5 inherits):** the western line stone is 220 yards from the floor's middle; the floor is 26 of Cael's yard-strides across; the den is under the floor's EASTERN lip; so den to the western line is about 233 yards and den to the eastern perimeter about 207. The protected round is 1,374 yards and a piece (sixty-two cords and twenty strides); radius ten cords; the constant offset is six and a half feet per cord. NO cord length and NO stride length is stated, and none is to be added. "A hundred and fifty yards inside" is dropped from the plan.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:445:- **The trials at the line** ran Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira, Oryn. Lira's full burst became one step; her words on stepping back out are the protected clock line. Oryn has crossed twice (with Brom; with the six) and reads nobody inside; her eight solo crossings are Movement 5's. Seln's map memory is Movement 5's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:453:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial, cold read, source-distance (4 tracked passages; one dense scene, ch30 scene 2), plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — seven applied by the coordinator, including the three protected units the author had correctly left as markers). Same-author repair r1 in progress when this block was written; the CLOSED note follows when the recheck returns.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:477:- **What each of the five reports inside** (beyond the protected lines): Karis can see where sixteen points would go and "can't find the hand to reach with"; this is not being empty ("reserve present, sigil gone"). Brom: "There's no next room"; a hundredweight weighs the same. Seln: "It is not there to be asked." Lira: a yard and a half, and no crack. Oryn: the surface count stops at "Four—"; returns at the stride; and stops when she alone is inside with Brom's wrist held across the line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:485:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: the three markers are replaced by the protected units (ch25:43, ch25:131, ch29:169); Teague took a fence on the 89th (the upper inn's paddock, three days, five marks); Seln's locked case is on its strap on him at the ford, out of Thornwater's loft and over the line, shut; all eleven Ring sheets are finished (the tenth torn and done over); the bands run round the foot of each upright and no band on the lip is described; the den is found from above, at the box, and Seln speaks first; Cael's overrun is three quarters of an hour; Cael does not watch Lira's step. Word counts, metrics and line numbers elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures.*
