editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:516:- **Correct Ring geometry:** western line stone to floor centre is 220 yards as printed; the floor is 26 of Cael's yard-strides across; the den is at the eastern lip. Therefore den to the western objective line is about 233 yards, and den to the eastern perimeter is about 207 yards. Do not reintroduce M4's discarded 150-yard figure (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:43-45,165-169,199-201`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:64-66`). The cord is approximately 21.9 yards by the protected circumference/radius figures, but its length and Karis's stride remain unstated (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:191-209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:531:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the seven audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Pike speaks unasked, to the open ledger); Seln's case carried on the page (Oxhollow's ford; the east gate; ch30's gear); four tracked passages restaged, the ch30 floor scene re-entered on the bands (Lira sees writing from the turf; the lip found when Brom's cord will not lie down; nine chips rejected and three families tried); ch28's survey proved once; two anchors; a cadence pass. Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES** — three applied by the coordinator: **Teague's fence is the axe-head hold's longer fence on the east road, forty marks, HOLD** (the repair's paddock job removed), and **Cael's overrun on the 96th is ONE quarter of an hour** (the repair's three quarters and the torn tenth sheet removed). Ruled KEEP: the cut bands run round the FOOT of each of the eleven uprights, a hand above the floor; no band on the lip; eleven finished, numbered sheets. All four tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 36 protected. 37742 words. No markers remain.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:538:- **Shadow has been used ONCE and remains sealed.** Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln had the sightline; Oryn was screened and saw him arrive, not come; the pack is no witness. Oryn cannot identify Seln as its source. Seln struck Cael's second reason for silence ("I shall not be a reason… I should sooner have her told what may be done to her than be used to keep her ignorant") WITHOUT offering to be known as the source: Movement 6 tells her sources by Path, not by person, and the seal serves again at the Stair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:541:- **The tenth fragment — Tide-adjacent — was acquired on the 100th** in Oryn's long reading (minute twenty-one); the notice is exact; "More than one" is said. **Cael let it happen without telling her first, with the covenant written beforehand, and told her the minute it was over. The page treats it as a wrong he did knowingly**: all four companions named it for what it is, he agreed that refusing would be right, and he chose against it. Writing it first made it knowing, not permitted. Oryn does NOT yet know the mechanism: her own naming of what was done, her terms and its cost to him are Movement 6's first scene. Integration cost is not yet paid.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:546:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial, cold read, source-distance (10 tracked passages; one dense scene, ch34 scene 3; one of the ten is now a restored protected unit), plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — 21 applied by the coordinator, including the four protected units the author had left as markers). Same-author repair r1 in progress when this block was written; the CLOSED note follows when the recheck returns.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:558:- **Injuries, as fixed on the page:** Lira, left forearm bitten through between wrist and elbow, held about thirty counts, never shaken; mended in an hour at the line; eight small pink marks; slung in a strip of Thornwater's blanket, the hand under the opposite collarbone. Right ankle over outward a third time; taped on the 97th; flat-footed, whole sole. Karis, throat pressed by her own fists under the jaws; knuckles skinned; no voice on the 96th–97th; a croak on the 98th; single rasped words on the 99th. Brom, a straight cut across the pads of four fingers of ONE hand [corrected at close: the protected unit gives one hand, four finger-pads]; mended at noon on the 97th; nothing drawn until the hundredth. Cael, left calf opened along the old seam on a stone in the rut; bound by Karis in a blanket strip that stayed on until Thornwater's yard on the 99th (never bound or mended by Oryn) [corrected at close]; counting eleven strides on the 97th, about forty by the evening of the 98th, none by noon of the 99th; a pale seam "four days, counting the one it went on". Left forearm struck in the second lock; dead to the elbow that night; back to the wrist on the 99th. Ribs: the tape off in the yard on the 99th. Seln: nothing. Oryn: spent to the bottom on the 96th; two mendings at noon on the 97th; none on the 98th or 99th.
