editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:7:Source of record for events: `books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-01.md` … `chapter-24.md` (≈118,400 words, spliced and closed 2026-09-04; prose governs where it differs from `CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md`, and the book-scope seams repairs of 2026-09-04 are part of the prose). Canon: `universe/` (bible, rules, ledger), `series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md`, `craft/NAME_REGISTRY.md`, `craft/VOICE_CHARTER.md` (Reader Standard). Run notes used for decisions already taken: `v3-runs/book-07/STATE_RUNNING.md` (per-chapter state; EXC-B7-001…005; the book-scope pass), `v3-runs/book-07/SERIES-FIT.md`, `v3-runs/book-07/audits/seams-read.md`. Seams read: edition Book 6 chapters 48–60, with the AFTER MOVEMENT 8 and AFTER MOVEMENT 9 coordinator rulings/CLOSED notes governing the entry; Book 8 Ch1 governs the exit. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A1] Book 8 (`v3-runs/book-08/DECISIONS-B7-RECONCILIATION.md`) is built on Book 7's closed prose, so Book 7's ending state and every line Book 8 quotes are protected (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:40:- **Teague:** "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew (four plus an older healer of no Path) stays at Lowmarch through the cold term. He has given the axe-head hold's long fence (forty, HOLD) to the five for the cold term. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch24 — OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:129:**Physical challenge or learning encounter per movement:** M1 the wash recovery, the hold drilled, the Thornwater stretch walked at dusk · M2 the ford (developed fight), the well, Lira's first runs on a stiff ankle · M3 the fan haul, the bench, the stampede (terrain fight), the lip · M4 the perimeter walk and the six trials inside the line (a learning encounter for every one of the six) · M5 the Ring (central set piece), the deep reading · M6 **the deliberate quieter movement:** the bowman's one-armed shooting lessons, Cael relearning the Wind economy in Thornwater's yard under the listening, and the strata demonstration · M7 the run to the stair, the stalemate, the ascent and the rim · M8 the wyrm trials and the Hall, then the walk home into first snow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:131:**Why M6 is quiet:** it holds the integration cost of the first non-combat fragment, the midpoint disclosure (Lira first, then six) and the birthday. Its action is learning. The book has just spent the Ring (M5) and is about to spend the Stair (M7). Lira's shooting arc keeps a body in motion and plants the Hall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:143:| **Oryn** | 9,200 (3.1%) | M3: 2,600 (Oxhollow's gate north, days 84–92: the hand she owed, the child three stops on, "a patient I want to read whole"; she puts a day on the route) · M6: 2,000 (day 100, the stool after the telling, the book on her knee: being a patient's source) · M6: 1,800 (days 111–112, the road north after leaving her mule with the crew; ends before Millrace's table) · M8: 2,800 (days 122–~128, the gap to Thornwater, the old woman's knee, writing the letter; ends on its four lines) | Her route, its arithmetic and debts; her city and why she left; her hands' findings; from day 100, the mechanism as told; the line's rule, which she tested alone; what she felt in him | Any theory of what he is or why the Quiet does not touch him ("I'm a healer, not a theorist"); the still place before he tells her (day 120); the content of Karis's hypothesis; anything about the Compact beyond what was said at a table; any sentimental declaration — her register breaks once, at the Hall, in Cael's POV |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:146:| **Karis** | 7,400 (2.5%) | M2: 1,400 (day 58, the cart-yard: "everybody knows", and not asking) · M4: 1,400 (night of day 95 at the stone: writing a stride, not a hypothesis) · M6: 2,600 (the week of tables: the tally of kinds she will not say; *the Quieting* chosen as grammar; the pen held over the page) · M8: 2,000 (days 119–120 at the far fire: the three centres, the edge laid and moved; ends on the pencil stopping) | Method; every number; her shelves; the strata; that she holds a hypothesis; that she is afraid of it | **The content of the hypothesis** (Book 8/9 territory) — the window stops her pen exactly as the page does; [UNBOUND] (used once, aloud, in the Ch15 equivalent, and never in her head); any who/why for the floors or the line |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:147:| **Lira** | 7,600 (2.5%) | M2: 1,800 (day 53, the bar at dusk without Wind: fast, with nothing at the end) · M3: 1,800 (day 78, the ledge: the burst her body chose; "That was me. The loud thing.") · M5: 2,000 (days 97–98: one arm, the order, "Later" kept; walking flat-footed because Oryn said) · M6: 2,000 (the bowman's lessons: shooting braced, one-armed, with a bow somebody else spans) | Everything she knows (the log, the fragments); her Fenmark and Norhold history; her want; her body's counts | Why Cael's fragments work inside before he tells her (day 110); any escalation of Cael–Lira past what the source shows (warmth and covenant, not declaration); asking for the ankle twice |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:148:| **Vastin** | ≈300 (0.1%) | M6, the Ch16 equivalent, verbatim in substance (§10) | A courtesy copy, read twice, filed as not understood | Anything else: no departure, no classified history, no age stated, no second window |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:150:**Per-movement secondary share:** M1 3,300 (10%) · M2 3,200 (9%) · M3 5,800 (15%) · M4 2,600 (7%) · M5 4,000 (11%) · M6 8,700 (24%) · M7 4,600 (12%) · M8 8,100 (21%). Book total ≈40,300 (13.4%). The book-level 87/13 is the target that binds. M6 and M8 run window-dense because Oryn is off the road in both, and the windows follow her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:156:Formula §5: the protagonist gets **≈135 growth beats** (4.5 per 10k; one about every 2,200 words), spread evenly with a slight middle bump. By movement: M1 14 · M2 15 · M3 17 · M4 18 · M5 19 · M6 18 · M7 17 · M8 17. By thirds that is ≈42 / 48 / 45. Supporting characters get many small beats each (0.1–0.7 per 10k = 3–21 over the book). No deuteragonist.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:178:**Density targets** (≈58 per 10k overall, front-loaded about 1.7x): **first third ≈81 per 10k** (M1 ≈82, M2 ≈82, M3 ≈78); **middle third ≈48** (M4 ≈50, with the line's mechanics taught as trials; M5 ≈42, with the acquisition spike; M6 ≈40); **final third ≈46** (M7 ≈40, M8 ≈55 with the inventory and the map). After M4 the system surfaces only at genuine turns: the notice, the self-readings, the rim, the fixed point, the inventory.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:191:| **Pressure, Ember, Blade, Storm** | M5 spent as noise in the run (Ember one point held out; Storm seeding the rut; Blade ringing with nothing to cut); M7 the Daeva suite on the rim (Wind, Storm, Compression, Ember) | Storm is the heaviest thing he owns and resettles round any new arrival (M6, heard for the first time) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:192:| **Tide-adjacent (NEW, the tenth)** | M5 day 100 the deep reading; **the notice** (verbatim, §10); M6 cost: three days of *listening*, not pulling (his own current at the edge of thought; the nine audible as flows); the idle state learned by the third night; **the first self-reading** (a place near the middle that does not flow; location only; not named); M7 ask refused at the lean-to, granted on the road; the first reading of another person (Oryn: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things); M8 the second and third self-readings; **"the still place"** (the phrase appears first here); told to Oryn with his hand on her wrist; **Teague not read** | Contact only; surface at a count of ten, deep only with the subject still, whole and willing; does nothing in a fight; *ask first, every time*; "Things you keep touching don't heal" |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:193:| **The anomaly → the still place** | M1–M5: "Still open. Still real. Patience." M6: the three words retired, with the reason. M8: a location. **Not a fragment; never counted; not the Quiet** | No theory, name-as-explanation, or *before/source/primordial* |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:196:**Others' progression:** Lira learns to be fast with nothing at the end (M2), and learns to shoot braced one-armed (M6 → M8). Brom learns Iron Skin is a shout out here, and what he is without it ("a big man with good footwork and a lip of fused stone"). Karis learns to keep one point; the lattice line across a mountain; the wall along a line from her knees. Seln learns that his Path "was never most of what I do." Oryn: what her hands can and cannot do at a line, tested eight times alone. Teague: a column he does not have.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:215:| M6 | Lira's shooting lessons; the Wind economy relearned under the listening | 2 × 1,500 | Learning |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:232:**The source's refrains:** Read the source for events, not sentences. It leans on a handful of refrains: "catalogued," "which was a ledger line," "which from Seln was a whole report," "a stride and a half," "the voice for a distance / an inventory," "filed," "the shelf," "did not have a column for it," and "which was, from X, a paragraph." Keep a few as character signatures (Cael catalogues; Pike reads things twice; a stride and a half is Oryn's distance). Thin the rest hard. Protected lines (§10) are exempt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:238:## 10. Protected wording (verbatim; later books quote or call these back)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:295:- Ch24, the inventory: *Ten confirmed fragments.* / *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — the Bronze from Ardenmere. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — Seln; source protected; the seal held past the Line as it held inside, and was used twice out here where no one who could carry it west could see it, and that is the seal's whole logic and it is unchanged. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; opened a door on a rim and held a floor in a hall, and I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people and have used it twice this year, once each way. Blade-adjacent — Ephram. Tide-adjacent — Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; the tenth, and the first that does nothing in a fight, and the only one whose engagement field says clinical, and the only one with a rule on it in her hand and mine: ask first, every time. Deployment notes current on all ten.* / *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.* / *Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map.* — **Audio rule:** Feryn's name never appears in a list run beside Oryn's; every inventory says "the Bronze from Ardenmere."
