   298	
   299	She sat. The boy bent his back.
   300	
   301	The stock lay across her knee, and it was a great deal livelier there than it had been on a rail. Her knee breathed. Her heart went through it. And under the wool her left arm came up at once to hold the thing steady, as it would have gone to a lath, or a wrist; it reached the knot, and she told it no, and it went on asking through every one of the eight.
   302	
   303	She put one in the ring.
