    36	
    37	"I'm only saying that it's a number. You don't stamp one bar thirty-one and stop."
    38	
    39	"That is the fourth sentence," said Karis. "I do not know what it counts."
    40	
    41	"I'm not asking you to know. I'm asking whether you've thought it."
    42	
    43	"I have thought of very little else for two nights." Karis rolled the leaf and tied it. "And I shall go on not writing it down."
    44	
