    48	
    49	"With our names on," said Brom.
    50	
    51	"With five strokes for a name, and a count of six."
    52	
    53	Karis laid the roll in the middle box, by itself, at one end, a little apart from the name and the five rows and the founding stone, as a person sets down on a bench the one tool that belongs to somebody else's trade.
    54	
