    56	
    57	She would not call the fifth a finding at all.
    58	
    59	It was the evening of the hundred and ninth day, with the light gone from the shutter and the hold's lantern standing on the trestle among the chips. She had asked the four of them to stay down after the day's slips were counted; and when they had settled, on kegs and sacks and the foot of the ladder, she let a good while go by before she spoke. She had three leaves laid side by side on the scrubbed board, and a fourth beside them, which was the rubbing of the founding stone.
    60	
