    87	He had one of his own, which had come to him at a camp by a stone, with an arm two hours old lying beside him, and he had written in Hesk's book that he would not invent a word for it. He had not gone back to that sentence since. He had only added to what stood under it: a tenth thing, and a place in the middle of himself that he was not yet free to speak of.
    88	
